{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>Here is your wife; take her and go.</b> And Avraham did not answer him, but we find that he did answer Avimelekh — that is what is meant by ״כי אמרתי פן אמות עליה״. And one may ask: since each of the two kings asked him, why did he answer the one and not answer the other? And it appears proper to say that Pharaoh, who said to him ״take and go,״ showed that he did not want Avraham's reply but only that he depart from before him, for he was the man on whose account the Holy One, blessed be He, had afflicted him with great plagues; therefore Avraham feared that if he delayed even a moment with a reply he might transgress the king's command. But in the matter of Avimelekh, who did not command him to leave, Avraham needed to remain and answer him, lest he appear to slight the king's honor if he did not respond to what he asked him:"], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:12:10.652338238Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}